-- Typechecks cleanly. The export answers, inside its own JUST, a list of n
-- numbers with a REFUSE as one more element. The rule's JUST takes a level of
-- the depth a directive reads, so the refusal is reached one element sooner
-- than in a bare list. `l4 run` and `l4 batch` must reach it for the same n.
@export the numbers in a MAYBE, then a refusal as one more element
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
`refusal in a MAYBE list` n MEANS JUST (`the numbers, then a refusal` n)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the numbers, then a refusal` n MEANS
  IF n EQUALS 0 THEN LIST (REFUSE "deep") ELSE n FOLLOWED BY `the numbers, then a refusal` (n MINUS 1)

#EVAL `refusal in a MAYBE list` 199
#EVAL `refusal in a MAYBE list` 200
